      <item>
       <widget class="QTextBrowser" name="textBrowser">
        <property name="plainText">
         <string>Land-use layer:
SE data is maintained at the highest resolution (regional planning model level) with 25,000 zones to allow portablity between TSM and other egional models.  However the model is run at the TSM level with ~8700 zones for run timeand resource efficiency.  This layer is regional planning level and during the run, prepratory steps are run to aggregate the data to TSM level (Yes, TSM zonal strucute is desiged to nest quite well with regional model zone structure and is updated on annual basis).

There might be instances where land-use data is updated for employment and other fields after running populationSIM and in all those instances, it's best to reproduce land-use files directly from this layer without needing to re-run POPSIM.

 Synthetic Household &amp; Population:
Outputs of POPSIM which reflect the Land-use layer.  This is assumed to go with the land-use file (Households and Population/ GQ).

Skim File:
Produced from &quot;Skimmy&quot; Step.  DISTANCE table is required.  It is possible to expose the &quot;DISTANCE&quot; property where use many provide other vairables like  distance from congested skims or something of that nature,  however,  the user needs to edit UEC's (Excel spreadhseets &gt; data tab) and thus it is decided to no expose &quot;DISTANCE&quot; table for user control.  See   model API for details on thsi control. 

Telework:
The model is calibrated with several telework shares. During preCOVID-19 in 2019, the telework share was 7%-9% and durning peak COVID-19 in 2020, the telework share reached to  22%-23% in Flroida.   The difference is quite high to impact Toll facilities, particulalry congestion relief facilities like Express Lanes.  The telework share came down to 20% in subsequent years (2021 - 2023).  However,  in order to reflect project assumptions,  telework is now modeled as a range from 7% to 25%. </string>
        </property>
       </widget>
